Friday Update
* Trade Alert: Sold half Oracle calls for nice gain; buy WW and SBUX calls*=
&nbsp;Stocks choppy amid hope for stimulus package and tighter creditStocks=
 are swirling in choppy midday trading on Friday, as worries over the prosp=
ects of tightening financial conditions weighed on the broader markets.The =
Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 201 points, or 0.64%, to 31,200.71. The S=
&amp;P 500 gained 19 points, or 0.51% to 3,848.63 and the Nasdaq Composite =
rose 197 points, or 1.49%, to 13,317.64At current levels, the Dow is set fo=
r its first weekly decline in four weeks while the S&amp;P and the Nasdaq a=
re heading for their first declines in two weeks. Still, they are sitting n=
ot too far from the record levels struck earlier this month on hopes of the=
 injection of another $1.9 trillion stimulus to the economy.On Friday, Morg=
an Stanley economists said January economic data has largely beat expectati=
ons, pointing to stronger-than-expected growth in Q1. They said another fis=
cal package expected to be passed and a gradual re-opening of the economy s=
hould further support personal income and spending."We lift our tracking es=
timate for 1Q21 GDP growth from 7.3% Q/Q annualized growth to 8.1%," the ec=
onomists said in a note.Meanwhile, Salesforce (CRM) fell 4.4% after its gui=
dance of flat margin in fiscal 2022 took the shine off a higher sales forec=
ast. "We believe CRM shares are likely to remain range bound over the near =
term and until it can close the Slack deal and begin proving out the synerg=
ies as questions about demand for Salesforce's products and sustainability =
of margin expansion have arisen over the past 3-6 months," said Oppenheimer=
 analyst Brian Schwartz in a note.In contrast, Etsy (ETSY) jumped 13% after=
 its Q4 results and revenue guidance outpaced market expectations, sparking=
 many price target upgrades, including from Goldman Sachs and Canaccord. "W=
ith four quarters of triple-digit growth, and the strongest new buyer growt=
h within our coverage we see Etsy as well-positioned to hang on to its gain=
s and continue to take share of ecommerce," said Wedbush analyst Ygal Aroun=
ian.Portfolio: Our Cigna March 210 calls were sold earlier this week for a =
51.3% overall gain=E2=80=A6 We sold first half of our ORCL calls today for =
a 27% gain, which is great. =E2=80=A6. We have two new ideas for you.*CURRE=
NT RECOMMENDATIONSOracle Corp. (ORCL) March $60 calls-- Symbol: ORCL210319C=
00060000-- Bought at $5.15 on Feb. 22-- Sold half today at $6.55 for 27.4% =
gain!-- Now trading at $5.90-- Sell second half at &nbsp;$7.50 lmt gtc-- Se=
t stop at $5.30 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*NEW RECOMMENDATIONSWW In=
ternational (WW) March 27.50 calls-- Symbol: WW210319C00027500-- Order: Buy=
 at $2.70 lmt day only-- If filled, set up to sell half at $3.55 lmt gtc an=
d half at $4.60 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at $1.90 stp, good after 10:3=
0 a.m. ET only&nbsp;*Starbucks Corp. (SBUX) March 105 calls-- Symbol: SBUX2=
10319C00105000-- Order: Buy at $4.20 lmt day only-- If filled, set up to se=
ll half at $5.50 lmt gtc and half at $7.15 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at=
 $2.95 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Thanks for reading,Jon D. Markman=
